{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-callbacks_and_events-javascript-repair-01","problem":"Repair the implementation below. Export exactly one function, `runEventSequence`, with `module.exports = runEventSequence`.

`runEventSequence(events, handlers, done)` processes events in array order. Each event has `type` and `payload`. For an event, invoke the listeners in `handlers[event.type]` in array order. A listener receives `(payload, acknowledge)` and signals completion by calling `acknowledge(value)`. Do not begin the next listener until the current listener acknowledges. After an event's listeners finish, append `{ type, acknowledgements }` to the result. Events without listeners produce an empty acknowledgements array. After every event finishes, call `done(results)` exactly once.

Each invocation must keep its progress and results isolated, so overlapping asynchronous invocations cannot reset or corrupt one another. Assume every listener calls its acknowledgement callback exactly once.

Use only standard JavaScript. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, packages, or frameworks. Return a corrected complete source file.

```javascript
let nextEventIndex = 0;
let collected = [];

function runEventSequence(events, handlers, done) {
  nextEventIndex = 0;
  collected = [];

  function advanceEvent() {
    if (nextEventIndex === events.length) {
      done(collected);
      return;
    }

    const event = events[nextEventIndex++];
    const listeners = handlers[event.type] || [];
    const acknowledgements = [];
    let listenerIndex = 0;

    function advanceListener() {
      if (listenerIndex === listeners.length) {
        collected.push({
          type: event.type,
          acknowledgements
        });
        advanceEvent();
        return;
      }

      const listener = listeners[listenerIndex++];
      listener(event.payload, function acknowledge(value) {
        acknowledgements.push(value);
        advanceListener();
      });
    }

    advanceListener();
  }

  advanceEvent();
}

module.exports = runEventSequence;
